Stage 27 — Common Jetpack Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating Jetpack libraries as business logic.

Ignoring dependency injection scopes.

Following generated Hilt code instead of dependency graphs.

Confusing Flow, LiveData, and UI state ownership.

Ignoring lifecycle-aware behavior.

Analyzing individual libraries without reconstructing the overall architecture.



---

Stage 28 — Jetpack Application Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify the Jetpack libraries used by an Android application and understand their architectural roles.

✅ Reconstruct Activities, Fragments, ViewModels, repositories, persistence, navigation, dependency injection, and background work.

✅ Analyze lifecycle-aware state management, asynchronous execution, and cross-library interactions.

✅ Distinguish handwritten business logic from Jetpack infrastructure and generated code.

✅ Validate architectural understanding through runtime observation.

✅ Produce comprehensive documentation describing the application's Jetpack-based architecture, execution model, dependency graph, and feature workflows.



